cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "CNNs for Intracranial Aneurysm Detection on TOF-MRA"
abstract: >-
  Code for a master's thesis on intracranial aneurysm detection in TOF-MRA
  with exam-level labels: a DICOM to NIfTI/MIP data pipeline, a 2D/3D CNN
  training engine with patient-grouped cross-validation, and a zero-shot
  nnU-Net baseline with a score-level ensemble. No data or trained weights
  are included.
authors:
  - family-names: Schenberg
    given-names: Bruno
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24350820
date-released: 2026-11-18
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bruno-schenberg/aneurysm_cnn"
keywords:
  - intracranial aneurysm
  - TOF-MRA
  - deep learning
  - medical imaging
  - maximum intensity projection
